build/
dist/

# Raw source books for the knowledge base (docs/KNOWLEDGE_SOURCES.md).
# These are personal reference copies used as ingestion input, not
# redistributed as part of the package (DESIGN.md section 11.1, 22).
#
# Note that excluding the PDFs is not by itself sufficient. Chunked full
# text is in substance the book, so what ingestion produces is NOT
# blanket-safe to commit: only citations (page ranges, headings, hashes)
# and non-invertible vectors go into src/syzygy/resources/knowledge/.
# See docs/adr/0003-ship-derived-knowledge-index-without-source-text.md.
docs/*.pdf

# Local application data. All Syzygy user data (profiles, natal charts,
# readings) lives in one SQLite database under platformdirs's user-data
# directory (src/syzygy/config.py), which is outside this repository by
# default. These patterns exist as a backstop in case a future dev/test
# workflow points the database at a repo-local path - profiles created
# while testing the prototype must never be committed.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
/data/
/.syzygy/

# Working notes written while using the app. Feedback is transcribed into
# TASKS.md as planned work; the scratch file itself is not history.
/feedback.md
